ogles2: the texture parameters VC4's TMU lacks, in the shader (docs/PI3_PLAN.md
§2.1): ARB_texture_mirror_clamp_to_edge, EXT_texture_lod_bias,
SGIS_texture_lod's base level and LOD range, EXT_texture_filter_anisotropic.
The sampler key gets lod_bias, lod_clamp and aniso (bits beside
force_first_level), and five uniform types follow QUNIFORM_UNIFORMS_ADDRESS:
the texture's LOD bias, min and max LOD (in level 0's terms) and level 0's
width and height. A wrap mode of PIPE_TEX_WRAP_MIRROR_CLAMP_TO_EDGE takes the
coordinate's absolute value (the library sets the TMU's clamp); the bias is
added to the shader's (or to an explicit LOD), or written alone as the TMU's
bias; with lod_clamp or aniso (fragment shaders, not cube maps) the LOD is
computed from the coordinates' derivatives in texels (GL's rho), the lookup
made with it explicitly (BSLOD) and clamped; aniso takes 2^aniso lookups
spread along the major axis, the LOD from the major axis over their number
but not below the minor axis's, and averages them. ntq_emit_tex's lookup
(the request and its result, patch 0018's planes too) is ntq_tex_lookup,
storing its results as it makes them. With none of the new key bits set the code is
the same as before. Mesa's own state makes none of these keys (its uniform
writer gives neutral values); v3dglslc compiles them from keys (-k, patch
0017). Applies after 0018.

